name: Go advisory scanner has honest experimental discovery and inspection
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_curation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_curation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART catalog
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: options govulncheck:scan
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | experimental-options
expect: Target
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | options-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | options-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | options-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | options-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | options-40x12
expect: Value:
ask: Is experimental support clear while the selected target setting remains readable at all six sizes, without launching scanner work?
resize: 120x36
submit: use govulncheck
require-live-snap: 20 Outside supported defaults | curated-default
expect: Experimental
expect: options govulncheck:scan
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | support-recovery-40x12
expect: options govulncheck:scan
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_curation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: Does default browsing explain experimental support and provide a readable settings action instead of treating the scanner as unknown?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: options govulncheck:scan
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | restored-options
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_curation.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: Does no-color restart retain honest support disclosure and unchanged source without scanner or model work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
